WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:05.430 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  the first memories i have as a kid  are the cozy italian sundays with my mom  at the movie theater  my favorite movie of them all was disney  fantasia  i watched lazy mickey mouse trying to  teach that broom how to clean the  sorceress cave and i thought to myself  how incredible it would be if all things  around me could simply come to life  if i could teach them to do all the  things i didn't want to do including  guess what tiding my room  mickey mouse's strategy seemed to be  working out pretty well  the room started cleaning the cave  autonomously and so happy and relieved  mickey simply went to sleep  there was really nothing to worry about  but a few hours later he wakes up to a  completely flooded cave  the rooms had been repeating the same  action over and over again without  realizing what was going on around them  so mickey begged them to stop  but it just won't listen  and so all he could do was tear them  apart  unfortunately a few hours later mickey  quickly realizes it's too late  he has lost control  this time more and more brooms start  invading the cave again desperately  trying to make it more clean  fast forward many years i find myself  often going back to the story as i try  to think about the role of artificial  intelligence in our society  these intelligent algorithms promise to  bring speed efficiency and effectiveness  but ended up making crucial decisions on  our everyday lives  who gets better education better health  care better financial support and who  goes to jail  but just like we don't expect that broom  to understand what we mean by clean  it's up to us to decide and teach those  algorithms what we mean by right  by fair and by good  the thousands of decisions of this kind  are made every day by data scientists  around the world  what data to use what to optimize for  and when a machine learning model is  accurate enough  well i am a data scientist and let me  tell you one thing  you should not trust me  and you should not leave it to  corporations governments or researchers  to make these decisions for you and not  because they intend harm  but because this is not a technology  problem this is a values problem  and i believe all of us should have a  say in the role of ai in our society  and let me show you why  in february 2019 nigeria parks was  arrested  he was accused of shoplifting and trying  to hit a police officer  turns out his face was identified using  a facial recognition software  but after 10 days in jail  the police found out that was a mistake  in august 2020 sharpie row is one of  thousands british students who saw their  college admissions revoked  the uk government had just started using  a new ai tool instead of final exams  that was penalizing struggling schools  in poor areas as opposed to elite  schools in wealthy areas  today  compass is one of the most widely used  ai tools in us criminal justice  so what compass does is it helps judges  determine whether a defendant should be  kept in jail or not while awaiting trial  and it does so by associating a score  from 1 to 10 to each defendant based on  more than 100 personal factors  if this score is high enough that  defendant will be jailed  but analyzing the behavior of this  algorithm showed that biased data coming  in produced biased results going out  let's take vernon and brisha for example  brisha committed minor prior fences and  no subsequent offense  yet as you can see her risk score is  much higher than vernon's  so what does fair mean to us in this  case  does it mean we want to apply the same  criteria to both of them  or does it mean ensuring that they're  both equally likely to be subject to  algorithmic  error because these two definitions are  equally valid but they have a very  different impact on society as a whole  so you see why deciding on rules and on  values it's so hard  because they mean different things for  every one of us  okay i know what you're thinking isn't  that why we elect our decision makers to  make these complex decisions for all of  us  well in theory that's true but the  problem with that is democracy is not  doing that well these days  in the past few years as a youth  activist i have worked hard with the  objective of involving as many young  citizens as possible in the democratic  lives of their communities  and i could see  how democracies are continuing to weaken  institutions appear distant  self-protective unreliable  only one in three americans trust their  elected officials  the political class struggles to  understand the complexity of technology  and to find consensus on the most  divisive matters of our time  we used to think that democracy happens  once every four years in a ballot but it  doesn't have to be this way  researchers and activists have studied a  new model of engagement in the past few  decades  deliberative democracy  and to see what that means let me take  you back to ireland 2015.  80 percent of the irish people approved  gay marriage in a referendum  but that journey started two years  earlier when the irish parliament was  facing a controversial issue for allen's  history and decided it was time to try  something new  so they called a convention on the  constitution composed of 66 ordinary  citizens and 33 members of the  parliament  they came together debated discussed and  some of those recommendations were that  turned into  referendums that became reality  so what happened here  well the world thought these citizens  were just too  polarized  distant and frankly incompetent to have  an impact they actually transitioned  from observers to decision makers  and you can see and you can hear how the  narrative changed from they the policy  makers to we the citizens  just like many activists around the  world that are doing already we can  influence the political agenda by  becoming good lobbyists for the causes  we believe in  deliberative democracy  can happen in many forms citizens  assemblies town halls participatory  budgeting and it has happened everywhere  in the world  from british columbia to kerala from  brazil to denmark from oregon to belgium  in italy politics per casa is trying to  activate the debate on climate change  and in california  citizens assemblies were proposed to  solve the problem of homelessness  i guess what you're thinking  this woman is trying to disrupt  our institutions as we know them for a  new topic direct democracy  couldn't be more wrong  i am suggesting we empower these  institutions every day with active  citizenry  so how can deliberative democracy really  help us design the role of ai in our  society  well first of all we'd have to define  and select a sample of citizens that can  be representative of our diversity  and then we need to set up the process  involve experts secure our decision  makers commitment  and decide the questions we want to  tackle because if we want to design a  new bill of digital rights we'll have to  agree on things like fairness  transparency openness explainability  we'll have to decide how data is  transferred and owned we'll have to  decide who audits who controls who  it will not be an easy process it will  require patience experimentation and  trust in the process even and most of  all when we don't agree with the outcome  but ultimately it'll help us understand  that beyond labels we're simply humans  i am very very passionate about ai i  really believe it can be an incredible  source of good for the world  could ai be the next decision maker  could ai find the best taxation policy  to optimize social welfare  or could we just leave it to ai to solve  climate change  maybe  we just don't know yet  but if and when  ai will be able to find those answers  we'll need to ask the right questions  and when ai will be able to find the  best solutions  we will need to agree on what we mean by  best  all of us should have a say in the role  of ai in our society  now i don't know how many of you have  seen disney fantasia but here's a little  spoiler for you  in the end the sorcerer comes in and  saves the day  but the role of ai in our society is no  mickey mouse game so please stay active  stay informed participate in your  democracy give it one more chance  because this time there will be no  sorcerer coming to save us  this time we cannot afford to go to  sleep  this time we can and we must write the  rules together  [Applause]  [Music]

